# General Angular rules

## Standalone components

- **Always use standalone components** - `standalone: true` for all new components
- **Explicit imports** - all dependencies must be explicitly listed in `imports: [...]`
- **Do not use NgModules** - use only standalone components

## Component structure

### Required

**All Angular components MUST contain:**
- ✅ `template` or `templateUrl` - component HTML template (REQUIRED)
- ✅ `styles` or `styleUrls` - component styles (REQUIRED)

```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-component-name',
  standalone: true,
  templateUrl: './component-name.component.html',  // REQUIRED
  styleUrls: ['./component-name.component.scss'],   // REQUIRED
  imports: [CommonModule, TranslatePipe, /* other imports */],
})
export class ComponentNameComponent implements OnInit {
  // Properties
  isResourceLoaded = false;
  protected readonly resource = 'path/to/strings';

  constructor(
    private readonly service: SomeService,
    private readonly destroyRef: DestroyRef,
  ) {
  }

  ngOnInit(): void {
    // Initialization
  }
}
```

### Alternative with inline template/styles

```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-component-name',
  standalone: true,
  template: '<div>...</div>',        // REQUIRED (if templateUrl not used)
  styles: ['.component { ... }'],    // REQUIRED (if styleUrls not used)
  imports: [CommonModule, TranslatePipe],
})
export class ComponentNameComponent {}
```

### Forbidden:
- ❌ Components without template/templateUrl
- ❌ Components without styles/styleUrls
- ❌ Empty styles arrays: `styles: []` (use at least an empty string or a file)

## Access modifiers

- **`private readonly`** - for all injected services in constructor
- **`protected`** - for methods and properties used in templates
- **`readonly`** - for constant properties (e.g. `protected readonly resource`)

## Subscription management

- **Always use `takeUntilDestroyed`** - for automatic Observable unsubscribe
- **Inject `DestroyRef`** - in constructor for subscription management
- **Do not use `ngOnDestroy`** - for unsubscribe; use `takeUntilDestroyed(this.destroyRef)`

Example:
```typescript
this.someService.getData$()
  .pipe(
    takeUntilDestroyed(this.destroyRef),
    finalize(() => this.isResourceLoaded = true),
  )
  .subscribe();
```

## Translation loading

- **`isResourceLoaded` pattern** - use to control translation resource loading
- **`protected readonly resource`** - for translation path (e.g. `'vacancies/strings'`)
- **Check before display** - use `*ngIf="isResourceLoaded"` in templates

Example:
```typescript
ngOnInit(): void {
  if (this.translationService.isResourceLoaded(this.resource)) {
    this.isResourceLoaded = true;
  } else {
    this.translationService.loadResource$(this.resource)
      .pipe(
        finalize(() => this.isResourceLoaded = true),
        takeUntilDestroyed(this.destroyRef),
      )
      .subscribe();
  }
}
```

## Routing

- **Lazy loading** - use `loadComponent` for all components
- **Lazy loading for child routes** - use `loadChildren` with exported constant
- **Path constants** - use `ROUTE_PATH` from `core/constants` for all paths

Example:
```typescript
export const vacanciesRoutes: Routes = [
  {
    path: '',
    pathMatch: 'full',
    loadComponent: () => import('./vacancies.component')
      .then((m) => m.VacanciesComponent),
  },
  {
    path: ':id',
    loadComponent: () => import('./vacancy/vacancy.component')
      .then((m) => m.VacancyComponent),
  },
];
```

## Typing

- **Interfaces for all data structures** - do not use `any`; create interfaces
- **Types for unions** - use `export type` for limited value sets
- **Nullable types** - explicitly use `| null` when value can be null

Example:
```typescript
export type LocationId = 'any' | 'us' | 'ua' | 'po' | 'cy';

export interface Vacancy {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  location?: LocationId;
}

vacancy: Vacancy | null = null;
```

## Data methods

- **`protected` methods** - for methods returning data for templates
- **Naming** - use `_items()` or `_data()` suffix (e.g. `row_16_items()`)

Example:
```typescript
protected row_16_items(): Vacancy[] {
  return vacancies;
}
```
